<title>JAPAN: Sumitomo Trust falls after suspension.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo Trust falls after suspension.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd fell on Thursday morning after the shares were suspended from trade on the previous day, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0057 GMT, the shares stood at 1,090 yen, having closed at 1,230 yen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The shares were suspended from trade on the Tokyo bourse on Wednesday due to unclear information concerning the issuance of preferred stocks. Company officials told a news conference that fund-raising was being considered but that specific details were undecided.</p>
</text>
